.TH PEINIT2 8 "September 2026" "Peios" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
peinit2 \- Peios real-root service manager and process 1
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peinit2
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peinit2
is the Peios real-root init process.  It prepares the required boot
infrastructure, starts the registry service, reads service definitions from
the registry, and supervises the resulting service graph.
.PP
The kernel starts
.B peinit2
as process 1.  It is not an interactive command and should not be started by
an administrator in an already-running system.
.PP
Service operations and system shutdown requests are submitted with
.BR svctl (8).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/peinit2
The service-manager executable.
.TP
.I /run/peinit/control.sock
The default service-control socket.
.TP
.I /run/peinit/jobs.sock
The default submitted-jobs socket.
.SH EXIT STATUS
As process 1,
.B peinit2
normally runs for the lifetime of the system.  A fatal boot or supervision
failure enters the configured recovery path rather than returning to the
kernel.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR svctl (8)
